{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-ado-1b/batch-conflict-first",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-ADO-1",
    "ADO-BATCH",
    "ADO-VALUES"
  ],
  "description": "ADO-BATCH conflict (another connection of the same process updates S of the first staged row): a client static batch-optimistic Recordset of SELECT ID, Code, V, V2, S FROM W ORDER BY ID is opened on a read/write copy; a second Connection runs \"UPDATE W SET S = 'ext' WHERE ID = 1\"; S of rows 1, 2 and 3 is then set to \"c1\", \"c2\", \"c3\"; UpdateBatch(adAffectAll) and the Errors; each row's Status, ID, S, OriginalValue and UnderlyingValue; Filter = adFilterConflictingRecords (RecordCount, rows) and Filter none; Resync(adAffectAll, adResyncUnderlyingValues), the rows again, a second UpdateBatch (Errors) and the rows; then the stored rows through Execute. Asks which staged changes reach the file, the per-row reporting and what a second submission does.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
  "pathBinding": "attempt-local-copy",
